WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:16,050
I listen to your talk on the summit. You mentioned the generational damage because we were bored with bad genes.

00:00:16,050 --> 00:00:22,050
Are those things that can be repaired with healthy lifestyle and future offspring will be okay.

00:00:22,050 --> 00:00:26,050
Plus ourselves, or can it never be reversed?

00:00:26,050 --> 00:00:34,050
Well, there are practitioners out there that say that you can change your genes by taking these supplements or doing these different things.

00:00:34,050 --> 00:00:38,050
But you can't, I just totally disagree with that.

00:00:38,050 --> 00:00:44,050
I'm open to it. Show me the proof. It's really easy to retest the person's genes.

00:00:44,050 --> 00:00:51,050
And you know, if you change that person's genetic picture, then, then great.

00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:54,050
There's never ever been the proof that that happens.

00:00:54,050 --> 00:01:00,050
Once you have a genetic gene defect, you are going to pass that on to your progeny.

00:01:00,050 --> 00:01:05,050
And there's, and that's the way it is.

00:01:05,050 --> 00:01:17,050
Now, if we were able to go back in time through some sort of magical apparatus and test our ancestors, I will guarantee that they did not have same number of defects that we have.

00:01:17,050 --> 00:01:22,050
So what causes our genetic defects is we inherit genetic defects from our parents.

00:01:22,050 --> 00:01:28,050
So if they have a double allele defect, you're going to inherit at least a single allele defect.

00:01:28,050 --> 00:01:32,050
Secondly, you acquire defects because of toxins.

00:01:32,050 --> 00:01:42,050
So you're exposed to benzines, you're exposed to pesticides, you're exposed to different chemicals that can affect those, you know, defects in, you know, cause a defect.

00:01:42,050 --> 00:01:46,050
And you're a set of people are 50 or punal pathways.

00:01:46,050 --> 00:01:55,050
And now, if you have children after that point in time that you caused that defect, you couldn't, and you could, they could inherit that defect from you.

